# ============================================================================
# Files whose BYTES are load-bearing, so git must not normalise their line
# endings on the way in or out.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# beta/legacy/ is the retired Scenarios\ORO_beta set. The uninstaller and the
# installer delete a file there only when it is BYTE-IDENTICAL to the copy we
# shipped (fc /b), so that anything the user edited is kept. Four of these came
# out of ORO-beta-260906.zip itself and three from the working tree - and one of
# them is LF while the rest are CRLF. Without this line a fresh clone would hand
# out a CRLF copy of that file, the compare would fail, and the migration would
# silently keep a scenario forever instead of retiring it. The bytes ARE the
# reference; they are never to be edited.
#
# beta/pics/ is launchpad artwork, shipped exactly as delivered - a 1920-wide
# shot is not re-encoded, so there is nothing for git to helpfully adjust.
# ============================================================================
beta/legacy/** -text
beta/pics/**   -text
